%% 1. Jev proposal - search responsibilities
flowchart TB
  Shopper["Shopper query"] --> Finder["Finder module inside Medusa application"]
  Finder --> Rules["Code: parse explicit numbers and currency<br/>Known filters and candidate text spans"]
  Rules --> Need{"Unresolved semantic question?"}
  Need -->|No| Contract["Code assembles and validates search contract"]
  Need -->|Yes| Jev["Jev: typed judgments<br/>Choice: occasion, theme, budget basis<br/>Select quantity / budget from candidate spans"]
  Jev --> Gate{"Required judgments meet tested thresholds?"}
  Gate -->|Yes| Contract
  Gate -->|Uncertain or no option fits| Clarify["Ask shopper to clarify<br/>Do not silently guess"]
  Clarify --> Shopper
  Jev -->|Timeout or API error| Fallback["Ordinary keyword and filter browse<br/>Preserve explicit constraints"]
  Fallback --> Contract
  Contract --> Search["Typesense retrieves and ranks catalogue candidates"]
  Search --> Commerce["Medusa checks regional prices<br/>Age/safety eligibility and sufficient sellable stock"]
  Commerce --> Results["Catalogue-grounded reasons and refine chips<br/>No-match or stock-shortfall explanation when needed"]
  Results --> Shopper
  %% Jev does not own prices, stock, safety rules or checkout.
  %% Provider credentials stay server-side. Failure is not a negative judgment.
  %% Truly free text may need a parser or generative model, evaluated separately.

%% 2. Jev proposal - example search contract
flowchart TB
  Query["Return gifts for 20 kids under INR 300 each"] --> Parse["Code finds candidate values<br/>20 and INR 300"]
  Parse --> Semantics["Jev resolves semantic roles when needed<br/>Occasion = return gift<br/>Quantity span = 20<br/>Budget span = INR 300<br/>Budget basis = per item"]
  Semantics --> Validate["Code normalises and validates<br/>quantity: 20<br/>budget amount: 300<br/>currency: INR<br/>basis: per_item<br/>age: unknown"]
  Validate --> Age{"Required age/safety information available?"}
  Age -->|No| Ask["Ask for age when necessary<br/>Unknown is not safety approval"]
  Ask --> Validate
  Age -->|Yes| Filters["Build hard filters<br/>Price within budget, age eligibility, quantity 20"]
  Filters --> Search["Typesense search"]
  Search --> Check["Medusa validates variant price and sellable quantity"]
  Check --> Display["Show matches and price scope<br/>Explain whether wrap/shipping are included"]
  Ambiguous["Under INR 300, without each"] --> Question["Clarify per-item versus total budget"]
  Question --> Query
  %% This is an example application contract, not Jev's native API response.
  %% Deterministic code may resolve explicit words such as each without Jev.

%% 3. Jev proposal - evaluation before adoption
flowchart LR
  Cases["Representative query set<br/>Clear / ambiguous budgets, age, quantity<br/>Missing attributes, unknown themes, timeouts"] --> Baseline["Existing extractor design<br/>Run against the same expected contracts"]
  Cases --> Candidate["Rules plus Jev candidate<br/>No production checkout authority"]
  Baseline --> Compare["Compare contract accuracy<br/>Clarification behaviour and invalid outputs<br/>End-to-end latency, cost and implementation effort"]
  Candidate --> Compare
  Compare --> Decision{"Meets agreed quality and latency targets?"}
  Decision -->|Yes| Review["Review evidence and approve adoption<br/>Then update architecture and technical plan"]
  Decision -->|No| Retain["Keep current approach or refine proposal"]
  %% No benchmark result, cost saving or faster implementation is claimed.
  %% Calibrate thresholds on representative examples; never treat confidence as proof.
